Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_release_of_nothing_held_moves_nothing`.

The defect: a release trusts its caller and walks the ancestors whether or not its region holds an
object of that kind, as the table did before it kept the per-region held count. It reads as
harmless, since every count saturates at zero, but a second release of one object takes a count a
child still holds, and an ancestor reports fewer live objects than it has.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(!released, "a release of nothing held was taken")`, from
any region of the tree.

diff --git a/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs b/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
index 10e92b9ae..98b072db4 100644
--- a/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
@@ -551,10 +551,7 @@ impl<const N: usize> RegionTable<N> {
             return true;
         };
         let held = &mut r.held[kind as usize];
-        if *held == 0 {
-            return false;
-        }
-        *held -= 1;
+        *held = held.saturating_sub(1);
         self.release(name, Counted::Object(kind));
         true
     }
